    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0060" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister
                        Churchill</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d8-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-31">31 May 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 546. Personal and top secret. From the President for the Former Naval
                    Person.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I should like very much to accept Dr. Churchill’s advice to make a sea voyage in
                    your direction and I hope to do so at a later date. Conditions here will not
                    permit it shortly after D plus 14 as suggested by you.</p>
                <pb facs="0061" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/>
                <p>Developments of the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Overlord</hi> campaign should
                    point with some accuracy to the time when a meeting of the Combined Staff is
                    necessary. I think we had best await developments of <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Overlord</hi> before making a decision as to the next full Staff
                    meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d8-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d8-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
